    {
      "id": "298f08b0-ca02-53c9-a1e6-27475df2f4ee",
      "name": "Workflow overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -720,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 600,
        "height": 1120,
        "content": "## Demo readiness for sales operations\n### How it works\nReconcile upcoming demo attendees with HubSpot before the meeting starts. A weekday schedule reads a dedicated Google Calendar, removes canceled events, declined attendees and internal domains, and gives recently created bookings a short grace period. Each remaining attendee is checked against the exact primary email in HubSpot. The workflow distinguishes no match, ambiguous matches, missing ownership and owners absent from the active directory. It never guesses an alternate email match.\n\nA stable event-and-attendee key updates a Google Sheets review queue. After the sheet succeeds, Slack receives one bounded digest of exceptions with calendar links. Healthy attendees are recorded without an alert. API failures and incomplete owner pagination stop the report instead of implying readiness.\n### Setup\n1. Connect Google Calendar, HubSpot App Token, Google Sheets and Slack credentials on their nodes. HubSpot needs contact and owner read access; invite the Slack bot to the destination channel.\n2. In Set config values, enter a dedicated demo calendar, your internal domains, spreadsheet ID, tab name and channel ID. Review the look-ahead window, booking grace and attendee limit.\n3. Create the sheet headers listed in the template setup, then run a manual check with test bookings. Use the workflow timezone for the weekday schedule.\n4. Filter the queue by checked_at for the current snapshot; older rows remain historical observations. Enable the schedule after reviewing the results.\n### Customization tips\nUse primary-email results as a review queue, not proof that a person is absent from the CRM. No attendee messages or CRM changes are sent."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
